# Three bounded local-oscillator pilots and their dispositions

2026-09-05. This lane follows the confirmed CMM/EPF collisions. No paper
number has been assigned and zero accepted seats are filled by this file.
The three rules were piloted before investing in an all-length proof;
alphabet values are parameters, not separately counted fresh systems.

The full finite carriers are cyclic words in {0,...,q−1}^n. Indices are
modulo n. The maximum boxes were q2:n≤10, q3:n≤8, q4:n≤6, q5:n≤5.
`probe_local_oscillators.py` and `PILOT_CANONICAL.txt` record every box,
not selected positive plots. Every full functional graph was traversed;
an independent generic local-constraint inverse was checked when q^n≤300.
This generic inverse decoder is only a control and gives no new theorem.

## OR: ordered reset, ternary focus retained for hostile Stage1 gate

```text
F_i=(x_i+1) mod q if x_i≤x_(i+1), else0.
```

The q3 pilot showed two qualitatively different recurrent families and
sharp-looking tail plateaus. Full proof pursuit yielded the literal
ternary contract, not a theorem for every q. The all-length theorem is
restricted to q=3; q>3 is parked without a claim or extra candidate count.
The OR contract specifies the entire forbidden21 image, each target's
2^occ01 independent-bit source set, all largest-fibre targets, complete
two-branch recurrent core and sharp tail3 floor(n/3)+1 for n≥3.

The run dynamics exposes a standard particle-parking mechanism rather
than hiding it. The source memo deducts this, Rule184, P169's smoothing
and labelled-window particle/hole mechanism, and coupled-oscillator
background. Retention means an independent gate is justified; it is not
an originality assertion or paper acceptance.

## AR: agreement reset, stopped

```text
F_i=(x_i+1) mod q if x_i=x_(i+1), else0.
```

At q2 the rule is exactly local NOR, and direct Boolean algebra gives
F³=R F (R the one-place left shift): if f(a,b)=¬(a∨b), then
f²_i=(x_i∨x_(i+1))∧(x_(i+1)∨x_(i+2))
      =x_(i+1)∨(x_i∧x_(i+2)); applying NOR once more gives
f³_i=¬(x_(i+1)∨x_(i+2))=f_(i+1).
Thus its one-step image lies in a rotation-driven polarity regime,
too close to the canonical antitone/polarity engine (P106 is a neighbor,
not a falsely asserted identical directed map).

The q≥3 pilots have increasingly irregular periods/tails; for example
q3,n8 has periods3,12,24 and maximum tail17. No all-parameter two-axis
spine was found in the bounded attempt. Disposition:
KILL_THIN_BINARY_POLARITY / NO_ALL_PARAMETER_HIGHER_ALPHABET_SPINE.
No conjectural high-q formula is carried into a manuscript.

## DA: disagreement advance, stopped after exact factor discovery

```text
F_i=(x_i+1) mod q if x_i≠x_(i+1), else x_i.
```

For d_i=(x_(i+1)−x_i) mod q in{0,...,q−1}, write e_i=1[d_i>0].
Since equality is exactly d_i=0, subtraction gives

```text
d_i' = d_i−e_i+e_(i+1).
```

This formula is an ordinary integer identity, not only a congruence:
when d_i=0 its right side is0 or1; when d_i>0 its right side lies
between0 andq−1. Therefore differences follow exactly the parallel
unit-service zero-range queue occurring in P169, up to orientation.
The global cyclic difference vector also satisfies sum d_i≡0 mod q;
the original phase remains a q-fold lift, so this factor is not claimed
to be a full literal conjugacy on words. Nevertheless no second
nontransferring inverse axis was found beyond this owned traffic factor
and phase reconstruction. Disposition: KILL_TRAFFIC_FACTOR_THIN.
No effort is spent decorating it with another rotor or sharp queue bound.

